  A pet salamander is one of the few pets that still uses its 
"special" attack when tame.  Monsters it wraps around take 
squeeze & fire damage (Subject to fire resistance).

From: <http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/mon1-343.txt>
(massively micro-edited):

SPECIES                LEV SPD  AC  MR  RESISTS   ATTACKS
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ ~~~ ~~~  ~~  ~~  ~~~~~~~~  ~~~~~~~

w          purple worm  15   9   6  20            2d8 E1d10d

:           salamander   8  12  -1   0  Fs        W2d8 1d6F H2d6 H3d6F

ATTACKS lists each of the monster's attacks.  The prefix letter,
if any, specifies how the attack is made:
      No letter means a direct attack
  H   Hugging or crushing
  W   Uses weapon

A suffix letter, if any, specifies the type of damage:
      No letter means normal physical damage
  F   Fire


 
  That's a total of 2d8 and 6d6 worth of damage per turn.  Should
average 24 points of damage per turn against non-fire-resistant 
monsters.  Speed of 12 is the equivalent of a slow player.
(Purple worm is speed 9.)  Try a wand of speed monster on it.

  AC of -1 means it's past the threshold where not only are the
number of hits reduced, but the damage from each hit is reduced
as well.

  It looks like a pretty good pet from here.  Keep it close by 
and it's like having a pet Firebrand.  Get it a good weapon and 
things look better still.

  Not sure if it eats.

  The big problem will be keeping alive monsters you want around,
e.g. nurses.


  Finally, its attack messages are pretty entertaining, if not
quite as much fun as hearing "BURRRP!" every so often.



